e point edge here but  rng was able to pick blue side first  because of their performance earlier in  the tournament and if you can't win  games on red side how are you gonna win  worlds now blue side did win every game  in this series and maybe poult truly  believes that had they played blue side  again the trend would have continued but  let's just be real here the draft that  we got in game 5 can't be completely  excused  and after all this was a response to a  question about the draft if you're a t1  fan there's a lot to like here even  though they lost msi they still play  second and the roster seems to be  getting stronger instead of stagnating  or something the young players around  faker will benefit from this experience  when they inevitably attempt to make  their run at worlds now to the west if  you're an n a fan eg's run to the semis  is one of the most exciting runs by an n  a team in some time and even though they  did get smashed once they arrived at the  semis the team is young and absolutely  packed with talent getting there at all  is an accomplishment for real but if  anything the expectations are even  higher now eg's dany actually tweeted  about how the season can be pretty  jam-packed if you're you know winning so  hopefully they figure out a way to  balance it all and come back stronger  now g2 started strong in the rumble  stage going 4-0 with wins against teams  like rng and t1 but things kind of fell  apart from there they only won one of  their next five games and the slump  continued into the bracket stage where  t1 casually swept them aside 3-0 though  they had a rough finish i think a semi's  appearance for this team was important  hopefully they get some data about this  international competition and their  analysts and coaches can come away with  some answers for them the next time they  face off this msi was one of the most  interesting i can remember and  even at a tournament that can constantly  surprise you as a fan and a viewer  